        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "versions.patch(\"/:id\") updates template_version content with `update template_version set content=..., extra=..., test_values=..., is_draft=... where id = ${ctx.params.id}` and no project_id/ownership predicate, and performs no prior lookup to confirm the version's parent template belongs to ctx.state.projectId. Every other template route in the codebase is scoped (e.g. templates.ts:85 `where project_id = ${ctx.state.projectId} and id = ${ctx.params.id}`), making this an isolated omission. Any authenticated user can overwrite another tenant's prompt template version \u2014 which the SDK then serves to that tenant's production LLM calls via the /v1/template_versions/latest route. Missing authorization check on a state-changing route.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived independently from source. packages/backend/src/api/v1/templateVersions.ts:66-74 performs `update template_version set content/extra/test_values/is_draft ... where id = ${ctx.params.id}` with NO project_id or template-ownership predicate, and the handler never references ctx.state.projectId nor does any prior lookup tying the version to the caller's tenant. The route is reachable: mounted at api/v1/index.ts:42 behind the globally-applied authMiddleware (backend/src/index.ts:34); PATCH /v1/template_versions/:id is NOT in publicRoutes (only /v1/template_versions/latest is, auth/utils.ts:73), so any valid JWT reaches it. The tenancy check at auth/utils.ts:117-127 runs only `if (ctx.state.projectId)` and validates only the ATTACKER'S OWN ?projectId= query param against their org \u2014 it never constrains the row being updated, and omitting the param skips it entirely. No compensating control exists: grep for ROW LEVEL SECURITY / current_setting / set_config across packages/ returns no matches, and the route has no per-route guard. Exploitation is trivial because db/init.sql:163 declares `template_version.id serial primary key` \u2014 sequential integers, enumerable rather than guessable. Impact chain verified: templateVersions.ts:24-34 (/latest) serves tv.content scoped by the victim's project id to the SDK, so an attacker-overwritten version is fed into the victim tenant's production LLM calls. Graph reachability is unusable here (all nodes in this file report reachable_from_entry=false, including the known-live SDK /latest route \u2014 an arrow-function under-linking artifact), so reach was confirmed against source instead; this is not evidence against exploitability. One correction to the analyst: the claim that this is an \"isolated omission\" is wrong \u2014 templates.ts:113-132 (POST /:id/versions) is also unscoped and templateVersions.ts:43-55 (GET /:id) reads any version unscoped; this broadens rather than weakens the finding. Exploit-reference check returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\", so no published-module/version comparison was possible; this verdict rests entirely on source evidence, not on any exploit catalog claim."
