prefix \"/datasets\" (datasets/index.ts:10) -> v1 prefix \"/v1\" (v1/index.ts:19) -> v1.use(datasets.routes()) (v1/index.ts:39) -> app.use(v1.routes()) (src/index.ts:41), with app.use(authMiddleware) at src/index.ts:34. (4) THE OMISSION IS A GENUINE DEVIATION, not authz-delegated-elsewhere: the same file/module enforces the control on siblings \u2014 patch(\"/:id\") line 105 includes `and project_id = ${projectId}`, and getDatasetById (datasets/utils.ts:6) and getDatasetBySlug (datasets/utils.ts:44) both filter by project_id. (5) I did NOT accept the graph's reachable_from_entry=false: my own query shows ALL 86 route registrations under api/v1/ are false (100%, including the plainly-live datasets.get(\"/\")), i.e. the known koa-router arrow-function under-linking artifact with no evidential weight; the frontend actively calls these routes (frontend/utils/dataHooks.ts:542-606), proving they are live. CORRECTIONS TO THE ANALYST: the regex is at line 76 (62 is the array declaration, not the regex); and the analyst under-scoped the surface \u2014 delete(\"/:id\") at 111-117 (`delete from dataset where id = ${id}`) is likewise predicate-free and public, allowing unauthenticated destruction of an entire dataset. Severity is CRITICAL rather than merely cross-tenant because id-unguessability does not mitigate it: authMiddleware:82 sets projectId from an unauthenticated query param, so GET /v1/datasets/<slug>?projectId=<victim-project-uuid> returns prompt_id and variation_id via getDatasetBySlug, which then feed the unprotected read/update/delete routes. exploit_search was unavailable (\"corpus unavailable: not indexed\"), which is advisory-only and immaterial for first-party code with no pinned component version."
